cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these models, please cite them as below.
title: "Browser models for: The direct benefit of a second modified live core vaccine dose for adult shelter dogs and cats"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kreisler"
    given-names: "Rachael"
    affiliation: "College of Veterinary Medicine, Midwestern University"
  - family-names: "DeTar"
    given-names: "Lena"
    affiliation: "Maddie's Shelter & Community Medicine, Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine"
  - family-names: "Mavrovouniotis"
    given-names: "Michael L."
    affiliation: "Social Compassion in Legislation"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://guidelines.jsmcah.org/adult-second-dose/
repository-code: https://github.com/jsmcah/adult-second-dose
date-released: 2026-10-31
abstract: "Interactive browser models that estimate the second doses of modified live vaccine a shelter gives per case averted in adult cats (panleukopenia) and dogs (distemper, parvovirus), from a shelter's own length-of-stay records and case counts or from illustrative stays, and the effect of the day the second dose is given. They accompany the modeling paper of the same title."
